    "created_at": "2018-02-12T15:41:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-02-12T15:41:00Z",
    "body": "Interesting. The redirect-limit hit seems to match what Chrome does when Location is some nonsense characters like \"#invalidurl:\" or \"\\b\", so maybe the spec is not so off. That's why the WPT test redirect-location.https.html https://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/third_party/WebKit/LayoutTests/external/wpt/fetch/api/redirect/redirect-location.js?l=43&rcl=2676595f0db73d5f35359dd4a33fd8b98122bd7c is so slow in Chrome (the invalid URL test redirects to itself).\r\n\r\nI'm not sure what the other browsers are doing in that test.",
